routes.what:
Free local photogrammetry on the owner's RTX 5070, used for:
- bark sections, giving tileable albedo, normal and height;
- trunk bases and root flares, reusable across trees;
- dense clipped evergreen shells: boxwood balls, sheared yew, the Smaragd column, as base shells that leaf-card 'fur' from R1 then covers;
- mulch, soil and stone ground surfaces;
- possibly hosta clumps.

Version 2.0 added built-in AI foreground masking for turntable scans. A radiancefields article advises at least 10 GB VRAM for it; the RTX 5070 has 12 GB. Version 2.1.1 exports COLMAP with masks, feeding R5 splat training.
